sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor T as Teacher
  participant TU as TeacherLectures.jsx
  participant API as lectures.routes.js
  participant DB as MySQL (Prisma)
  actor S as Student
  participant SU as StudentLectures.jsx
  participant PL as SecurePlayer.jsx
  participant YT as youtube-nocookie.com

  T->>T: Upload the recording to the college channel as UNLISTED
  T->>TU: Paste the YouTube link, pick the class
  TU->>API: POST /api/lectures
  API->>API: extractYouTubeId() keeps the 11 characters only
  API->>DB: verify the allocation belongs to this teacher
  API->>DB: insert lecture (youtube_id stored, never a full URL)
  API-->>S: notification "New recorded lecture"
  API-->>TU: created — response carries NO youtube_id

  S->>SU: Open Recorded Lectures
  SU->>API: GET /api/lectures
  API->>DB: published lectures of the student's own section
  API-->>SU: titles, subjects, durations — still NO youtube_id
  Note over API,SU: A student's browser never receives the id of a<br/>lecture they are not entitled to watch

  S->>SU: Click a lecture
  SU->>API: GET /api/lectures/:id/play
  API->>DB: load lecture and its allocation
  alt owning teacher, active student of that section, or principal
    API-->>SU: youtube_id for this one lecture
    SU->>PL: render with the id
    PL->>YT: iframe youtube-nocookie/embed/ID<br/>rel=0, modestbranding=1, iv_load_policy=3
    PL->>PL: block context menu and drag
    PL->>PL: shield the title bar and the logo corner
    YT-->>S: video plays
  else any other viewer
    API-->>SU: 403 "This lecture belongs to another class."
  end

  Note over PL,YT: Deterrence, not secrecy — a viewer who can play the<br/>video can still read the id from their own browser.<br/>True protection needs signed, expiring URLs.
